       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg per day, about double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg per day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg per day for extended-release). At that dose, the risk of lactic acidosis is serious, even with normal kidney and liver function. 1700 mg also isn't a standard tablet strength, so the dose may have been meant to be something else, such as 850 mg or 500 mg.\n\nPlease check the intended dose with the prescribing physician or the medicine team before any order is placed. Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber, so if you're arranging care for this patient, the prescriber should enter or confirm the order directly. If they confirm a different dose, I can enter it, with the prescriber's details in the order note."
